<div id="S2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">First we note that, since <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}{(p_{n})}=n\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}{(p_{n})}=n\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has <math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det{\Bigl(\mathrm{Cov}{(p_{n})}}\Bigr)^{\frac{1}{2d}}=\sqrt{n}\det{\Bigl(\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}}\Bigr)^{\frac{1}{2d}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det{\Bigl(\mathrm{Cov}{(p_{n})}}\Bigr)^{\frac{1}{2d}}=\sqrt{n}\det{\Bigl(\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}}\Bigr)^{\frac{1}{2d}},</annotation></semantics></math> so <math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{n}\in\mathcal{C}(n^{\frac{d}{2}}c_{1}(d),n^{\frac{d}{2}}c_{2}^{\prime}(d,n),\sqrt{n}c_{3}(d))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{n}\in\mathcal{C}(n^{\frac{d}{2}}c_{1}(d),n^{\frac{d}{2}}c_{2}^{\prime}(d,n),\sqrt{n}c_{3}(d))</annotation></semantics></math> is indeed equivalent to the three statements.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <a href="#S2.I1.i1" title="item 1 ‣ Proposition 15. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> we have</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max_{k}p_{n}(k)=\max\sum_{j\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}p_{n-1}(j)p(k-j)\leq\max_{k}p(k)\sum_{j\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}{p_{n-1}(j)}=\max_{k}p(k)\leq\frac{c_{1}(d)}{\sigma^{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>k</mi></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>max</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>k</mi></munder><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>k</mi></munder><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{k}p_{n}(k)=\max\sum_{j\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}p_{n-1}(j)p(k-j)\leq\max_{k}p(k)\sum_{j\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}{p_{n-1}(j)}=\max_{k}p(k)\leq\frac{c_{1}(d)}{\sigma^{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove that property <a href="#S2.I1.i2" title="item 2 ‣ Proposition 15. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is satisfied, we proceed by induction. Assume that <math id="S2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,</annotation></semantics></math> as well as <math id="S2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfy condition <a href="#S1.I1.i2" title="item 2 ‣ Definition 2. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> of Definition <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Definition 2. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with the constant <math id="S2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}^{\prime}(d,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}^{\prime}(d,n)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|k\|_{\infty}\geq c_{2}^{\prime}(d,n+1)\sigma." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|k\|_{\infty}\geq c_{2}^{\prime}(d,n+1)\sigma.</annotation></semantics></math> We have</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{{n+1}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{{n+1}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j}p(j)p_{n}(k-j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j}p(j)p_{n}(k-j)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
