<p id="S2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="S2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{d}\leq e^{\frac{x}{2c}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{d}\leq e^{\frac{x}{2c}},</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq 2cd\bigl(\log{(2cd)}\bigr)^{2},d\geq 1,c\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq 2cd\bigl(\log{(2cd)}\bigr)^{2},d\geq 1,c\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.
On the other hand, the second double sum in (<a href="#S2.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) is</span></p>
