<p id="S2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">where (<a href="#S2.E22" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) holds at least as long as (<a href="#S2.E19" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) is satisfied since <math id="S2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq\|k\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq\|k\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and similarly for the last inequality.
Plugging the bounds (<a href="#S2.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>), (<a href="#S2.E23" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>) in (<a href="#S2.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) we obtain</span></p>
