<p id="S2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="S2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}^{\prime}(d,n+1)=3\cdot 4^{d+1}c_{2}(d)c_{2}^{\prime}(d,n)^{2}=\bigl(3\cdot 4^{d+1}c_{2}(d)\bigr)^{2^{n}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}^{\prime}(d,n+1)=3\cdot 4^{d+1}c_{2}(d)c_{2}^{\prime}(d,n)^{2}=\bigl(3\cdot 4^{d+1}c_{2}(d)\bigr)^{2^{n}-1}</annotation></semantics></math> by the inductive hypothesis. Note that this choice of <math id="S2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}^{\prime}(d,n+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}^{\prime}(d,n+1)</annotation></semantics></math> also ensures that (<a href="#S2.E19" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) is satisfied and therefore the proof of <a href="#S2.I1.i2" title="item 2 ‣ Proposition 15. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. is complete.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">For property <a href="#S2.I1.i3" title="item 3 ‣ Proposition 15. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, let <math id="S2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a random vector with p.m.f. <math id="S2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{X}=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{X}=p</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}:=\sum_{i=1}^{n}{X_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}:=\sum_{i=1}^{n}{X_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. copies of <math id="S2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, has p.m.f. <math id="S2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. We observe that</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}}{|p_{n}(k)-p_{n}(k-e_{i})|}=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\|p_{S_{n}}-p_{S_{n}+e_{i}}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}}{|p_{n}(k)-p_{n}(k-e_{i})|}=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\|p_{S_{n}}-p_{S_{n}+e_{i}}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">For any probability measures <math id="S2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1},\mu_{2},\nu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1},\mu_{2},\nu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the total variation distance satisfies the convolution inequality</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mu_{1}\ast\mu_{2}-\nu_{1}\ast\nu_{2}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\|\mu_{1}-\nu_{1}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}+\|\mu_{2}-\nu_{2}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mu_{1}\ast\mu_{2}-\nu_{1}\ast\nu_{2}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\|\mu_{1}-\nu_{1}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}+\|\mu_{2}-\nu_{2}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">This can be proved either directly or by the fact that total variation is an <math id="S2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f-</annotation></semantics></math>divergence and therefore satisfies a data processing inequality.
Choosing <math id="S2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}=\nu_{1}=p_{S_{n-1}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}=\nu_{1}=p_{S_{n-1}},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{2}=p_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{2}=p_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{2}=p_{X+e_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{2}=p_{X+e_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|p_{S_{n}}-p_{S_{n}+e_{i}}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\|p_{X}-p_{X+e_{i}}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|p_{S_{n}}-p_{S_{n}+e_{i}}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\|p_{X}-p_{X+e_{i}}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">Using the assumption on <math id="S2.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, the last inequality yields</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{d}\|p_{S_{n}}-p_{S_{n}+e_{i}}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\sum_{i=1}^{d}\|p_{X}-p_{X+e_{i}}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\frac{c_{3}(d)}{\sigma}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{d}\|p_{S_{n}}-p_{S_{n}+e_{i}}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\sum_{i=1}^{d}\|p_{X}-p_{X+e_{i}}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\frac{c_{3}(d)}{\sigma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 16</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a random vector with p.m.f. <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying conditions <a href="#S1.I1.i2" title="item 2 ‣ Definition 2. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <a href="#S1.I1.i3" title="item 3 ‣ Definition 2. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> of Definition <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Definition 2. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Let <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(n)}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(n)}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. uniform random vectors on the cube <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Denote by <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{n}^{(d)}(x)=\prod_{i=1}^{d}h_{n}(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{n}^{(d)}(x)=\prod_{i=1}^{d}h_{n}(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> the density of <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and by <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{n}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{n}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math> the density of <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(n)}+X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(n)}+X</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall z\in[0,1]^{d},\forall n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall z\in[0,1]^{d},\forall n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,
</span><math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\in\{0,\ldots,n-1\}^{d}}h_{n}^{(d)}(j+z)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in\{0,\ldots,n-1\}^{d}}h_{n}^{(d)}(j+z)=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=k+z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=k+z</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> where </span><math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,  </span><math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f_{n}^{(d)}(x)-p(k)|\leq\frac{2^{d-1}}{d}\frac{c_{3}}{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f_{n}^{(d)}(x)-p(k)|\leq\frac{2^{d-1}}{d}\frac{c_{3}}{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with </span><math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{3}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> the constant that appears in condition </span><a href="#S1.I1.i3" title="item 3 ‣ Definition 2. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a><span id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of Definition </span><a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Definition 2. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a><span id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=k+z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=k+z</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I2.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> where </span><math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I2.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I2.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, with </span><math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|k\|_{\infty}\geq c_{2}\sigma+n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|k\|_{\infty}\geq c_{2}\sigma+n</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I2.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
