<div id="S2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we prove 1.
Let us prove that the one-dimensional case holds i.e.
<math id="S2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}h_{n}(j+z)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}h_{n}(j+z)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="S2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. For this, one does an induction on <math id="S2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="S2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}=U_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}=U_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1}(z)=1_{[0,1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1}(z)=1_{[0,1]}</annotation></semantics></math> so the base case is immediate.
Let us suppose by induction that the claim holds for <math id="S2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. Noticing that the support of <math id="S2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,n]</annotation></semantics></math> and using the induction hypothesis, we get</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j=0}^{n}h_{n+1}(j+z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j=0}^{n}h_{n+1}(j+z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=0}^{n}\int_{0}^{1}h_{n}(j+z-u)du=\sum_{j=0}^{n}\left(\int_{0}^{z}h_{n}(j+z-u)du+\int_{z}^{1}h_{n}(j+z-u)du\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>z</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=0}^{n}\int_{0}^{1}h_{n}(j+z-u)du=\sum_{j=0}^{n}\left(\int_{0}^{z}h_{n}(j+z-u)du+\int_{z}^{1}h_{n}(j+z-u)du\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=z+\int_{0}^{z}h_{n}(n+z-u)du+\int_{z}^{1}\left(\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}h_{n}(k+1+z-u)\right)du=z+1-z=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>z</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=z+\int_{0}^{z}h_{n}(n+z-u)du+\int_{z}^{1}\left(\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}h_{n}(k+1+z-u)\right)du=z+1-z=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
