<p id="S2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the <math id="S2.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional case, observe that since <math id="S2.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{n}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{n}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math> is a product, for all <math id="S2.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\in\{0,\ldots,n-1\}^{d}}h_{n}^{(d)}(j+z)=\sum_{j\in\{0,\ldots,n-1\}^{d}}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{d}h_{n}(z_{i}+j_{i})\right)=\prod_{i=1}^{d}\left(\sum_{j_{i}=0}^{n-1}h_{n}(z_{i}+j_{i})\right)=1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in\{0,\ldots,n-1\}^{d}}h_{n}^{(d)}(j+z)=\sum_{j\in\{0,\ldots,n-1\}^{d}}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{d}h_{n}(z_{i}+j_{i})\right)=\prod_{i=1}^{d}\left(\sum_{j_{i}=0}^{n-1}h_{n}(z_{i}+j_{i})\right)=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">where, for the last equality, we have used the above one-dimensional argument.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us prove the second item. Using item <a href="#S2.I2.i1" title="item 1 ‣ Lemma 16. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, one has</span></p>
<table id="S2.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{n}^{d}(x)-p(k)=f_{n}^{(d)}(k+z)-p(k)=\sum_{i\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}p(k-i)h_{n}^{(d)}(i+z)-p(k)=\sum_{i\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}u(i)v(i)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{n}^{d}(x)-p(k)=f_{n}^{(d)}(k+z)-p(k)=\sum_{i\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}p(k-i)h_{n}^{(d)}(i+z)-p(k)=\sum_{i\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}u(i)v(i),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(i)=p(k-i)-p(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(i)=p(k-i)-p(k)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(i)=h_{n}^{(d)}(z+i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(i)=h_{n}^{(d)}(z+i)</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that the sum actually ranges over <math id="S2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,\ldots,n-1\}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,\ldots,n-1\}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{n}^{(d)}(i+z)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{n}^{(d)}(i+z)=0</annotation></semantics></math> outside this discrete cube. Also, for <math id="S2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=(i_{1},\dots,i_{d})\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=(i_{1},\dots,i_{d})\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, denote</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(i):=\left(T(v)\right)_{i}=\sum_{j\geq i}v_{j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(i):=\left(T(v)\right)_{i}=\sum_{j\geq i}v_{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p13.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p13.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq i</annotation></semantics></math> means that <math id="S2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{l}\geq i_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{l}\geq i_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq l\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq l\leq d</annotation></semantics></math>. By a straightforward induction,</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(i)=(T^{-1}(W))_{i}=\sum_{\epsilon\in\{-1,1\}^{d}}\left(\prod_{j=1}^{d}\left(-\epsilon_{j}\right)\right)W\left(i+\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{\epsilon_{k}+1}{2}e_{k}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(i)=(T^{-1}(W))_{i}=\sum_{\epsilon\in\{-1,1\}^{d}}\left(\prod_{j=1}^{d}\left(-\epsilon_{j}\right)\right)W\left(i+\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{\epsilon_{k}+1}{2}e_{k}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p13.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p13.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let us introduce the standard dot product
in <math id="S2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{2}(\mathbb{Z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{2}(\mathbb{Z})</annotation></semantics></math> as
<math id="S2.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle z,h\rangle_{l^{2}(\mathbb{Z})}:=\sum_{i\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}z(i)h(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle z,h\rangle_{l^{2}(\mathbb{Z})}:=\sum_{i\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}z(i)h(i)</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S2.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z,h\in\mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z,h\in\mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the sum
<math id="S2.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}u(i)v(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}u(i)v(i)</annotation></semantics></math>
can be rewritten as <math id="S2.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle u,T^{-1}W\rangle_{l^{2}(\mathbb{Z})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle u,T^{-1}W\rangle_{l^{2}(\mathbb{Z})}</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{-1}:=\sum_{\epsilon\in\{-1,1\}^{d}}\left(\prod_{j=1}^{d}(-\epsilon_{j})\right)S_{\epsilon}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{-1}:=\sum_{\epsilon\in\{-1,1\}^{d}}\left(\prod_{j=1}^{d}(-\epsilon_{j})\right)S_{\epsilon},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p13.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p13.5.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S2.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is the left-shift operator, that is, <math id="S2.p13.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(S_{\epsilon}W\right)_{i}=W\left(i+\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{\epsilon_{k}+1}{2}e_{k}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(S_{\epsilon}W\right)_{i}=W\left(i+\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{\epsilon_{k}+1}{2}e_{k}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. It is well known that the adjoint <math id="S2.p13.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\epsilon}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\epsilon}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.p13.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>,
is the right-shift operator or in another words <math id="S2.p13.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S_{\epsilon}^{\star}(W))_{i}=W(i-\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{\epsilon_{k}+1}{2}e_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{\epsilon}^{\star}(W))_{i}=W(i-\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{\epsilon_{k}+1}{2}e_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}u(i)v(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}u(i)v(i)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}\sum_{\epsilon\in\{-1,1\}^{d}}u_{i}\left(\prod_{j=1}^{d}\left(-\epsilon_{j}\right)\right)W\left(i+\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{\epsilon_{k}+1}{2}e_{k}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}\sum_{\epsilon\in\{-1,1\}^{d}}u_{i}\left(\prod_{j=1}^{d}\left(-\epsilon_{j}\right)\right)W\left(i+\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{\epsilon_{k}+1}{2}e_{k}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle u,T^{-1}(W)\rangle_{l^{2}(\mathbb{Z})}=\langle\left(T^{-1}\right)^{\star}u,W\rangle_{l^{2}(\mathbb{Z})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle u,T^{-1}(W)\rangle_{l^{2}(\mathbb{Z})}=\langle\left(T^{-1}\right)^{\star}u,W\rangle_{l^{2}(\mathbb{Z})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}W(i)\sum_{\epsilon\in\{-1,1\}^{d}}\left(\prod_{j=1}^{d}(-\epsilon_{j})\right)u\left(i-\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{\epsilon_{k}+1}{2}e_{k}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}W(i)\sum_{\epsilon\in\{-1,1\}^{d}}\left(\prod_{j=1}^{d}(-\epsilon_{j})\right)u\left(i-\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{\epsilon_{k}+1}{2}e_{k}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
