<div id="Thmtheorem17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 17</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The upper bound of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem16" title="Lemma 16. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, item <a href="#S2.I2.i2" title="item 2 ‣ Lemma 16. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> depends on <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, but not on <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, for <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math> our new method of proof improves the bound <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, Eq. (21)]</cite> by removing the dependence on <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. the number of uniforms being added to the discrete random variable.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p15.1" class="ltx_p">We are ready to prove Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> will readily follow from this, together with the generalized EPI in <math id="S2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x)=x\log{\frac{1}{x}},x&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x)=x\log{\frac{1}{x}},x&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and note that <math id="S2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is increasing for <math id="S2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leq 1/e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leq 1/e</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote <math id="S2.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}{X_{i}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}{X_{i}},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S2.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(n)}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}{U_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(n)}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}{U_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S2.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{S_{n}+U^{(n)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{S_{n}+U^{(n)}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the density of <math id="S2.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}+U^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}+U^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> on the <math id="S2.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{S_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{S_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> the p.m.f. of <math id="S2.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S2.p16.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{S_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{S_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the three parts of Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem15" title="Proposition 15. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>. We have</span></p>
