<p id="S2.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">First, we bound the second term. From part <a href="#S2.I2.i3" title="item 3 ‣ Lemma 16. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem16" title="Lemma 16. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, in that range of <math id="S2.p16.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and for any <math id="S2.p16.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x\in k+[0,1)^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in k+[0,1)^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
