<p id="S2.p16.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p16.5.1" class="ltx_text">We show that the first term in (<a href="#S2.E28" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) is approximately <math id="S2.p16.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(S_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(S_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.
To that end we apply the estimate (<a href="#S2.E41" title="In Lemma 19 ([]). ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem19" title="Lemma 19 ([]). ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> to the integrand with <math id="S2.p16.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\Theta_{d,n}(\frac{1}{\sigma}),D=\Theta_{d,n}(\sigma^{2d-1}),M=\sigma^{2d},a=f_{S_{n}+U^{(n)}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\Theta_{d,n}(\frac{1}{\sigma}),D=\Theta_{d,n}(\sigma^{2d-1}),M=\sigma^{2d},a=f_{S_{n}+U^{(n)}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p16.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=p_{S_{n}}(k)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=p_{S_{n}}(k).</annotation></semantics></math> The assumption of the lemma is satisfied for an appropriate choice of the implied constants since by Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem16" title="Lemma 16. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> and part <a href="#S2.I1.i1" title="item 1 ‣ Proposition 15. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> of Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem15" title="Proposition 15. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>,</span></p>
