<p id="S2.p16.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p16.6.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, since there are at most <math id="S2.p16.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\sigma^{2d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\sigma^{2d})</annotation></semantics></math> elements in the set <math id="S2.p16.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}:\|k\|_{\infty}\leq\sigma^{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}:\|k\|_{\infty}\leq\sigma^{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
