<p id="S2.p16.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p16.7.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S2.p16.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{n}(k,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{n}(k,x)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem16" title="Lemma 16. ‣ 2 Proofs of main results ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> applied to the random variable <math id="S2.p16.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, which satisfies the assumption <math id="S2.p16.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{S_{n}}\in\mathcal{C}(c_{1}^{\prime}(d,n),c_{2}^{\prime}(d,n),c_{3}^{\prime}(d,n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{S_{n}}\in\mathcal{C}(c_{1}^{\prime}(d,n),c_{2}^{\prime}(d,n),c_{3}^{\prime}(d,n))</annotation></semantics></math> for some constants that depend on <math id="S2.p16.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d,n</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
