<div id="S2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the continuous EPI (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1.1 Monotonicity of entropy ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}{X_{i}+U_{i}}\Bigr)\geq h\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{n}{X_{i}+U_{i}}\Bigr)+\frac{d}{2}\log{\Bigl(\frac{n+1}{n}\Bigr)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}{X_{i}+U_{i}}\Bigr)\geq h\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{n}{X_{i}+U_{i}}\Bigr)+\frac{d}{2}\log{\Bigl(\frac{n+1}{n}\Bigr)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">and by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> applied to the differential entropies on both sides</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}{X_{i}}\Bigr)+O_{d,n}\Bigl(\frac{\log{\sigma}}{\sigma}\Bigr)\geq H\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{n}{X_{i}}\Bigr)+O_{d,n}\Bigl(\frac{\log{\sigma}}{\sigma}\Bigr)+\frac{d}{2}\log{\Bigl(\frac{n+1}{n}\Bigr)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}{X_{i}}\Bigr)+O_{d,n}\Bigl(\frac{\log{\sigma}}{\sigma}\Bigr)\geq H\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{n}{X_{i}}\Bigr)+O_{d,n}\Bigl(\frac{\log{\sigma}}{\sigma}\Bigr)+\frac{d}{2}\log{\Bigl(\frac{n+1}{n}\Bigr)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p19.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p19.3.1" class="ltx_text">But by (<a href="#S1.E9" title="In Remark 6. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), <math id="S2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{d,n}\Bigl(\frac{\log{\sigma}}{\sigma}\Bigr)=O_{d,n}\Bigl({H(X_{1})}{e^{-\frac{1}{d}H(X_{1})}}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{d,n}\Bigl(\frac{\log{\sigma}}{\sigma}\Bigr)=O_{d,n}\Bigl({H(X_{1})}{e^{-\frac{1}{d}H(X_{1})}}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>
and the result follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 18</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem18.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The rate can be improved to superpolynomial by splitting the sum according to <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{1+\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{1+\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> and optimising over <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 19</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmtheorem19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D,M\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D,M\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and, for <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&gt;0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math> consider <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(x)=F(x)-x\log{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(x)=F(x)-x\log{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x)=-x\log{x}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x)=-x\log{x}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Then, for <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq a,b\leq\frac{D}{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq a,b\leq\frac{D}{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\mu&lt;\frac{1}{e}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>e</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\mu&lt;\frac{1}{e},</annotation></semantics></math>
we have the estimate</span></p>
