<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section is devoted to the proof (see end of Section <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>) of the following result, which shows that discrete log-concave extensible random vectors with isotropic extension satisfy the properties of Definition <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Definition 2. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. In Section <a href="#S3.SS5" title="3.5 Relaxing the isotropicity assumption on 𝑓 ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> we show that this can be generalized to discrete log-concave extensible random vectors with almost isotropic extension.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem20" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 20</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem20.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem20.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem20.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is a centered log-concave p.m.f. on <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with isotropic extension and covariance matrix <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}=\sigma^{2}\mathrm{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}=\sigma^{2}\mathrm{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there are constants <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}(d),c_{2}(d),c_{3}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}(d),c_{2}(d),c_{3}(d)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\mathcal{C}\left(c_{1}(d),c_{2}(d),c_{3}(d)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\mathcal{C}\left(c_{1}(d),c_{2}(d),c_{3}(d)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, provided that <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=\det\left(\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}(p)\right)^{\frac{1}{2d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">det</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=\det\left(\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}(p)\right)^{\frac{1}{2d}}</annotation></semantics></math> is large enough depending on <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\left(c_{1}(d),c_{2}(d),c_{3}(d)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\left(c_{1}(d),c_{2}(d),c_{3}(d)\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in Definition <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Definition 2. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. That is, if <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is large enough depending on <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}p(k)\leq\frac{c_{1}(d)}{\sigma^{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}p(k)\leq\frac{c_{1}(d)}{\sigma^{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|k\|_{\infty}\geq c_{2}(d)\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|k\|_{\infty}\geq c_{2}(d)\sigma</annotation></semantics></math></p>
