</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Ball’s bodies</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In what follows, we set <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the volume of the unit Euclidean ball denoted by <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. For a given convex body <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> in its interior, its <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">inradius</span> <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(K)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the largest <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for which <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rB_{2}^{d}\subset K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rB_{2}^{d}\subset K</annotation></semantics></math> and its <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">circumradius</span> <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(K)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the smallest <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subset RB_{2}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subset RB_{2}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. The support function of <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{K}(x)=\max_{y\in K}\langle x,y\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{K}(x)=\max_{y\in K}\langle x,y\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and the radial function of <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{K}(x)=\inf\{t&gt;0;\ tx\in K\}=1/\|x\|_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{K}(x)=\inf\{t&gt;0;\ tx\in K\}=1/\|x\|_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x\|_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x\|_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the gauge associated to <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For most results in this section we will assume that <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a centered, isotropic, log-concave density, that is
<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f=1</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}xf=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}xf=0</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}x^{T}xf=\sigma^{2}\mathrm{I}_{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}x^{T}xf=\sigma^{2}\mathrm{I}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math>
To this function <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, we attach its Ball’s bodies.
This important family of bodies was introduced by Ball <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. We refer to the book <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> for the properties of these.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem21" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 21</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem21.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem21.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> be an integrable, centered log-concave function.
For any <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the set <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{p}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{p}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as follows</p>
<table id="S3.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{p}(f):=\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\int_{0}^{\infty}pr^{p-1}f(rx)dr\geq f(0)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{p}(f):=\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\int_{0}^{\infty}pr^{p-1}f(rx)dr\geq f(0)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem21.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Ball <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> established that the set <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{p}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{p}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex body. Moreover, its radial function is</p>
<table id="S3.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{K_{p}(f)}(x)=\Bigl(\frac{1}{f(0)}\int_{0}^{\infty}pr^{p-1}f(rx)dr\Bigr)^{\frac{1}{p}}\hskip 5.69046pt\text{for}\hskip 5.69046ptx\neq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>for</mtext><mo lspace="0.570em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{K_{p}(f)}(x)=\Bigl(\frac{1}{f(0)}\int_{0}^{\infty}pr^{p-1}f(rx)dr\Bigr)^{\frac{1}{p}}\hskip 5.69046pt\text{for}\hskip 5.69046ptx\neq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem21.p1.3" class="ltx_p">From integration in polar coordinates (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, Proposition 2.5.3]</cite>), it follows that <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{d+1}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{d+1}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> is centered and, for any <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{K_{d+p}(f)}|\langle x,u\rangle|^{p}dx=\frac{1}{f(0)}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|\langle x,u\rangle|^{p}f(x)dx." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{K_{d+p}(f)}|\langle x,u\rangle|^{p}dx=\frac{1}{f(0)}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|\langle x,u\rangle|^{p}f(x)dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem21.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Finally, the following inclusion relations between <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{p}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{p}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{q}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{q}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> hold <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, Proposition 2.5.7]</cite>, for <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\Gamma(p+1)^{\frac{1}{p}}}{\Gamma(q+1)^{\frac{1}{q}}}K_{q}(f)\subset K_{p}(f)\subset e^{\frac{d}{p}-\frac{d}{q}}K_{q}(f)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>q</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\Gamma(p+1)^{\frac{1}{p}}}{\Gamma(q+1)^{\frac{1}{q}}}K_{q}(f)\subset K_{p}(f)\subset e^{\frac{d}{p}-\frac{d}{q}}K_{q}(f).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem21.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Applying these inclusions first for <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=d+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=d+1</annotation></semantics></math> then for <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=d+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=d+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=d+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=d+2</annotation></semantics></math> and using classical inequalities on Gamma functions, it follows that there exist universal constants <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;c_{1}&lt;c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;c_{1}&lt;c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any dimension <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, one has</p>
<table id="S3.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}K_{d+1}(f)\subset K_{d}(f)\subset c_{2}K_{d+1}(f)\quad\hbox{and}\quad c_{1}K_{d+2}(f)\subset K_{d+1}(f)\subset c_{2}K_{d+2}(f)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}K_{d+1}(f)\subset K_{d}(f)\subset c_{2}K_{d+1}(f)\quad\hbox{and}\quad c_{1}K_{d+2}(f)\subset K_{d+1}(f)\subset c_{2}K_{d+2}(f).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We shall apply to <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{d+1}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{d+1}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> the following theorem due to Kannan, Lovász and Simonovits <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>, Theorem 4.1]</cite> to which we give a new and simple proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem22" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 22</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem22.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem22.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem22.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> be a centered convex body in <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S3.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{h_{K}(u)^{2}}{d(d+2)}\leq\frac{1}{|K|}\int_{K}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx=\langle\mathrm{Cov}(K)u,u\rangle\leq\frac{d}{d+2}h_{K}(u)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>K</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{h_{K}(u)^{2}}{d(d+2)}\leq\frac{1}{|K|}\int_{K}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx=\langle\mathrm{Cov}(K)u,u\rangle\leq\frac{d}{d+2}h_{K}(u)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(t)=|\{x\in K;\langle x,u\rangle=t\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(t)=|\{x\in K;\langle x,u\rangle=t\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote by <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-b,a]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-b,a]</annotation></semantics></math> its support. Then one has <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=h_{K}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=h_{K}(u)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(t)dt=|K|,\quad\int_{\mathbb{R}}tf(t)dt=\int_{K}\langle x,u\rangle dx\quad\hbox{and}\quad\int_{\mathbb{R}}t^{2}f(t)dt=\int_{K}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>K</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="1.000em">,</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mi>t</mi><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>K</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mtext>and</mtext><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>K</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(t)dt=|K|,\quad\int_{\mathbb{R}}tf(t)dt=\int_{K}\langle x,u\rangle dx\quad\hbox{and}\quad\int_{\mathbb{R}}t^{2}f(t)dt=\int_{K}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">We define <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)=\alpha\left(1+\frac{t}{da}\right)^{d-1}\mathds{1}_{[-da,a]}(t),\quad\hbox{where}\ \alpha=\frac{1}{a\left(1+\frac{1}{d}\right)^{d}}\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(t)dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)=\alpha\left(1+\frac{t}{da}\right)^{d-1}\mathds{1}_{[-da,a]}(t),\quad\hbox{where}\ \alpha=\frac{1}{a\left(1+\frac{1}{d}\right)^{d}}\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(t)dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">And let <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined by <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(t)=dh(-dt)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(t)=dh(-dt)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, it is not difficult to see that</span></p>
<table id="S3.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}}g(t)dt=\int_{\mathbb{R}}h(t)dt=\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(t)dt\quad\hbox{and}\quad\int_{\mathbb{R}}tg(t)dt=\int_{\mathbb{R}}th(t)dt=\int_{\mathbb{R}}tf(t)dt=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}}g(t)dt=\int_{\mathbb{R}}h(t)dt=\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(t)dt\quad\hbox{and}\quad\int_{\mathbb{R}}tg(t)dt=\int_{\mathbb{R}}th(t)dt=\int_{\mathbb{R}}tf(t)dt=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">We shall prove that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}}t^{2}g(t)dt\leq\int_{\mathbb{R}}t^{2}f(t)dt\leq\int_{\mathbb{R}}t^{2}h(t)dt," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}}t^{2}g(t)dt\leq\int_{\mathbb{R}}t^{2}f(t)dt\leq\int_{\mathbb{R}}t^{2}h(t)dt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">from which the inequality (<a href="#S3.E44" title="In Theorem 22. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>) follows immediately by a simple calculation.
If <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\neq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\neq g</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows from (<a href="#S3.E45" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) that there exist at least two points <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}(g)&lt;t_{2}(g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}(g)&lt;t_{2}(g)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g-f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g-f</annotation></semantics></math> changes sign at these points and, in the same way, if <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\neq h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\neq h</annotation></semantics></math> there exists at least two points <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}(h)&lt;t_{2}(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}(h)&lt;t_{2}(h)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f-h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f-h</annotation></semantics></math> changes sign at these points.
Since the function <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{1/(d-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{1/(d-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> is concave on its support <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-b,a]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-b,a]</annotation></semantics></math> and the functions <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{1/(d-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{1/(d-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1/(d-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1/(d-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> are affine on their respective supports <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-da,a]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-da,a]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-\frac{a}{d},a]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-\frac{a}{d},a]</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that the functions <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g-f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g-f</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f-h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f-h</annotation></semantics></math> have exactly two sign changes and that they are non positive on <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t_{1},t_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t_{1},t_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> and non negative outside <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t_{1},t_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t_{1},t_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us define <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> to be either <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g-f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g-f</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f-h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f-h</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for any <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t-t_{1})(t-t_{2})v(t)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t-t_{1})(t-t_{2})v(t)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Integrating this inequality, we deduce that <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int t^{2}v(t)dt\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int t^{2}v(t)dt\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We shall deduce from the preceding theorem the following important technical lemma. We note that Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem23" title="Lemma 23. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a> (and its consequences) is the only part, where the isotropicity assumption is used.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem23" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 23</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem23.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem23.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem23.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> be an integer. There exist two constants <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;C_{d}^{\prime}&lt;C_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;C_{d}^{\prime}&lt;C_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R_{+}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R_{+}}</annotation></semantics></math> centered, isotropic, log-concave density and for every <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{d}^{\prime}\leq\left(\int_{0}^{\infty}dr^{d-1}f(r\theta)dr\right)^{\frac{1}{d}}\leq C_{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{d}^{\prime}\leq\left(\int_{0}^{\infty}dr^{d-1}f(r\theta)dr\right)^{\frac{1}{d}}\leq C_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem23.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem23.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{d}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{d}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are constants depending only on the dimension <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. In fact, we may take</span></p>
<table id="S3.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{d}^{\prime}=\frac{c_{1}^{d+2}}{\sqrt{2\pi}e^{\frac{3}{2}}}\quad\hbox{and}\quad C_{d}=(d+1)c_{2}^{d+2}L_{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{d}^{\prime}=\frac{c_{1}^{d+2}}{\sqrt{2\pi}e^{\frac{3}{2}}}\quad\hbox{and}\quad C_{d}=(d+1)c_{2}^{d+2}L_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem23.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem23.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are the absolute constants appearing in (<a href="#S3.E43" title="In Definition 21. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The function <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> being isotropic, we have <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}(f)=\sigma^{2}I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}(f)=\sigma^{2}I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, for some <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int f=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int f=1</annotation></semantics></math>, thus <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{f}=\max(f)^{\frac{1}{d}}\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{f}=\max(f)^{\frac{1}{d}}\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that proving (<a href="#S3.E46" title="In Lemma 23. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>) is equivalent to proving that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{d}^{\prime}B_{2}^{d}\subset f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}K_{d}(f)\subset C_{d}B_{2}^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{d}^{\prime}B_{2}^{d}\subset f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}K_{d}(f)\subset C_{d}B_{2}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem22" title="Theorem 22. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a> to the centered body <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{d+1}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{d+1}(f)</annotation></semantics></math>, we get that for any <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{h_{K_{d+1}(f)}(u)^{2}}{d(d+2)}\leq\frac{1}{|K_{d+1}(f)|}\int_{K_{d+1}(f)}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx\leq\frac{d}{d+2}h_{K_{d+1}(f)}(u)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{h_{K_{d+1}(f)}(u)^{2}}{d(d+2)}\leq\frac{1}{|K_{d+1}(f)|}\int_{K_{d+1}(f)}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx\leq\frac{d}{d+2}h_{K_{d+1}(f)}(u)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we use (<a href="#S3.E42" title="In Definition 21. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) for <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=2</annotation></semantics></math> to get that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{K_{d+2}(f)}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx=\frac{1}{f(0)}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}f(x)dx=\frac{\sigma^{2}}{f(0)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{K_{d+2}(f)}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx=\frac{1}{f(0)}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}f(x)dx=\frac{\sigma^{2}}{f(0)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">This gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}^{d+2}\frac{\sigma^{2}}{f(0)}\leq\int_{K_{d+1}(f)}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx\leq c_{2}^{d+2}\frac{\sigma^{2}}{f(0)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}^{d+2}\frac{\sigma^{2}}{f(0)}\leq\int_{K_{d+1}(f)}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx\leq c_{2}^{d+2}\frac{\sigma^{2}}{f(0)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">Using again the inclusion relations (<a href="#S3.E43" title="In Definition 21. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>), we get upper and lower bound of <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|K_{d+1}(f)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|K_{d+1}(f)|</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|K_{d}(f)|=1/f(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|K_{d}(f)|=1/f(0)</annotation></semantics></math>, by (<a href="#S3.E42" title="In Definition 21. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) for <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, altogether we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}^{2d+2}\sigma^{2}\leq\frac{1}{|K_{d+1}(f)|}\int_{K_{d+1}(f)}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx\leq c_{2}^{2d+2}\sigma^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}^{2d+2}\sigma^{2}\leq\frac{1}{|K_{d+1}(f)|}\int_{K_{d+1}(f)}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx\leq c_{2}^{2d+2}\sigma^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p6.6.1" class="ltx_text">Using these inequalities, (<a href="#S3.E48" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>) and the inclusion relations (<a href="#S3.E43" title="In Definition 21. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>), we get</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\frac{d+2}{d}}c_{1}^{d+2}\sigma B_{2}^{d}\subset K_{d}(f)\subset\sqrt{d(d+2)}c_{2}^{d+2}\sigma B_{2}^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\frac{d+2}{d}}c_{1}^{d+2}\sigma B_{2}^{d}\subset K_{d}(f)\subset\sqrt{d(d+2)}c_{2}^{d+2}\sigma B_{2}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p6.7.1" class="ltx_text">From <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, Theorem 4]</cite>, we have <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(0)\geq e^{-d}\max(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(0)\geq e^{-d}\max(f)</annotation></semantics></math> hence</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{L_{f}}{e}\leq f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}\sigma=\left(\frac{f(0)}{\max(f)}\right)^{\frac{1}{d}}L_{f}\leq L_{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mi>e</mi></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{L_{f}}{e}\leq f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}\sigma=\left(\frac{f(0)}{\max(f)}\right)^{\frac{1}{d}}L_{f}\leq L_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p6.8.1" class="ltx_text">Using that
<math id="S3.SS1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{f}\geq 1/\sqrt{2\pi e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{f}\geq 1/\sqrt{2\pi e}</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>A concentration lemma</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following concentration lemma will be required to establish the concentration property 2.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem24" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 24</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Concentration Lemma)<span id="Thmtheorem24.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem24.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem24.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem24.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem24.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{d}:=3^{\frac{1}{d}}C_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{d}:=3^{\frac{1}{d}}C_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmtheorem24.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the constant from (<a href="#S3.E47" title="In Lemma 23. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>). Then, for every log-concave, isotropic, centered density function <math id="Thmtheorem24.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and for every <math id="Thmtheorem24.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmtheorem24.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x\|_{2}\geq c_{d}/f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x\|_{2}\geq c_{d}/f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)\leq f(0)2^{-\|x\|_{2}\frac{f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{c_{d}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)\leq f(0)2^{-\|x\|_{2}\frac{f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{c_{d}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\max}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\max}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a value where the maximum of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is attained and for every <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\max}(\theta)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\max}(\theta)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a value where the maximum of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\mapsto f(r\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\mapsto f(r\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is attained. Since <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave, for every <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the function <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\mapsto f(r\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\mapsto f(r\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is non-increasing for <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq r_{\max}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq r_{\max}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, for every <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}(\theta)\geq r_{\max}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}(\theta)\geq r_{\max}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\infty}dr^{d-1}f(r\theta)dr\geq\int_{r_{\max}(\theta)}^{r_{0}(\theta)}dr^{d-1}f(r\theta)dr\geq f(r_{0}(\theta))(r_{0}(\theta)^{d}-r_{\max}(\theta)^{d})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\infty}dr^{d-1}f(r\theta)dr\geq\int_{r_{\max}(\theta)}^{r_{0}(\theta)}dr^{d-1}f(r\theta)dr\geq f(r_{0}(\theta))(r_{0}(\theta)^{d}-r_{\max}(\theta)^{d}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">We choose <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}=r_{0}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}=r_{0}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="S3.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}(\theta)=\Bigl(2d\int_{0}^{\infty}{\frac{r^{d-1}f(r\theta)}{f(0)}dr}+r_{\max}^{d}\Bigr)^{\frac{1}{d}}\hskip 2.84544pt," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}(\theta)=\Bigl(2d\int_{0}^{\infty}{\frac{r^{d-1}f(r\theta)}{f(0)}dr}+r_{\max}^{d}\Bigr)^{\frac{1}{d}}\hskip 2.84544pt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">so that,
by (<a href="#S3.E50" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 A concentration lemma ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>), one has
<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(r_{0}(\theta))\leq\frac{f(0)}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(r_{0}(\theta))\leq\frac{f(0)}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\mapsto f(r\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\mapsto f(r\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is non-decreasing on <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,r_{\max}(\theta)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,r_{\max}(\theta)]</annotation></semantics></math>, one has</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{+\infty}dr^{d-1}f(r\theta)dr\geq\int_{0}^{r_{\max}(\theta)}dr^{d-1}f(0)dr=f(0)r_{\max}(\theta)^{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{+\infty}dr^{d-1}f(r\theta)dr\geq\int_{0}^{r_{\max}(\theta)}dr^{d-1}f(0)dr=f(0)r_{\max}(\theta)^{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">and therefore, by Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem23" title="Lemma 23. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\max}(\theta)\leq\frac{\big(d\int_{0}^{+\infty}r^{d-1}f(r\theta)dr\big)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}}\leq\frac{C_{d}}{f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\max}(\theta)\leq\frac{\big(d\int_{0}^{+\infty}r^{d-1}f(r\theta)dr\big)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}}\leq\frac{C_{d}}{f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by (<a href="#S3.E47" title="In Lemma 23. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>).
Thus, by (<a href="#S3.E51" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 A concentration lemma ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>) and the definition of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}(\theta)\leq\left(\frac{3}{f(0)}\right)^{\frac{1}{d}}C_{d}=\frac{c_{d}}{f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}(\theta)\leq\left(\frac{3}{f(0)}\right)^{\frac{1}{d}}C_{d}=\frac{c_{d}}{f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Since for every <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq r_{0}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq r_{0}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, one has <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}(\theta)=\frac{r_{0}(\theta)}{r}\cdot r+(1-\frac{r_{0}(\theta)}{r})\cdot 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}(\theta)=\frac{r_{0}(\theta)}{r}\cdot r+(1-\frac{r_{0}(\theta)}{r})\cdot 0</annotation></semantics></math>, by
log-concavity, we deduce</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(r)\leq f(0)\left(\frac{f(r_{0}(\theta))}{f(0)}\right)^{\frac{r}{r_{0}(\theta)}}\leq f(0)2^{-{\frac{r}{r_{0}(\theta)}}}\leq f(0)2^{-{\frac{rf(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{c_{d}}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(r)\leq f(0)\left(\frac{f(r_{0}(\theta))}{f(0)}\right)^{\frac{r}{r_{0}(\theta)}}\leq f(0)2^{-{\frac{r}{r_{0}(\theta)}}}\leq f(0)2^{-{\frac{rf(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{c_{d}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, if <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x\|_{2}\geq c_{d}/f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x\|_{2}\geq c_{d}/f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)\leq f(0)2^{-\|x\|_{2}\frac{f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{c_{d}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)\leq f(0)2^{-\|x\|_{2}\frac{f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{c_{d}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
