<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we will approximate the isotropic constant of an isotropic, log-concave density <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> in a discrete way. To do so, we will first approximate the integral as a sum and subsequently approximate the continuous covariance of <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> by its discrete covariance.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem26" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem26.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 26</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem26.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem26.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem26.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem26.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a log-concave isotropic density function with covariance matrix of the form <math id="Thmtheorem26.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}\mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}\mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}fdx-\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}f(k)\right|={O_{d}}\Bigl(\frac{1}{\sigma}\Bigr)\hskip 2.84544pt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}fdx-\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}f(k)\right|={O_{d}}\Bigl(\frac{1}{\sigma}\Bigr)\hskip 2.84544pt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us proceed by induction. Let us first consider the one dimensional base case. Let <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a log-concave function and let suppose that the maximum of <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is attained at <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}\in\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}\in\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}\leq x_{0}&lt;k_{0}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}\leq x_{0}&lt;k_{0}+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, one has</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}}fdx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}}fdx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex102.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}\int_{k}^{k+1}f(x)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}\int_{k}^{k+1}f(x)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{k&lt;k_{0}}f(k)+\sum_{k\geq k_{0}+1}f(k+1)+\min\{f(k_{0}),f(k_{0}+1)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{k&lt;k_{0}}f(k)+\sum_{k\geq k_{0}+1}f(k+1)+\min\{f(k_{0}),f(k_{0}+1)\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)-f(k_{0})-f(k_{0}+1)+\min\{f(k_{0}),f(k_{0}+1)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)-f(k_{0})-f(k_{0}+1)+\min\{f(k_{0}),f(k_{0}+1)\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)-\max\{f(k_{0}),f(k_{0}+1)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)-\max\{f(k_{0}),f(k_{0}+1)\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)-\max_{\mathbb{Z}}f." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>ℤ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)-\max_{\mathbb{Z}}f.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The reverse inequality is analogous and thus one gets</span></p>
<table id="S3.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\int_{\mathbb{R}}fdx-\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)\right|\leq\max_{\mathbb{Z}}f\leq\max_{\mathbb{R}}f." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>ℤ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>ℝ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\int_{\mathbb{R}}fdx-\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)\right|\leq\max_{\mathbb{Z}}f\leq\max_{\mathbb{R}}f.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we get <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\mathbb{R}}(f)=\frac{L_{f}}{\sigma}\leq\frac{1}{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\mathbb{R}}(f)=\frac{L_{f}}{\sigma}\leq\frac{1}{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>, by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, which proves the base case. Notice that the inequality (<a href="#S3.E53" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>) holds as soon as <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is quasi-concave on <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. if <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is first non-decreasing then non-increasing and not necessarily a density.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathbb{R}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathbb{R}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and let
<math id="S3.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(y):=\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x,y)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(y):=\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x,y)dx</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave as the marginal of a log-concave function. Moreover <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is an isotropic density and <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{R}^{d-1}}(F)=\sigma^{2}I_{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{R}^{d-1}}(F)=\sigma^{2}I_{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. One has</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x,y)dxdy-\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}f(k)\right|\leq\left|\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d-1}}F(y)dy-\sum_{y\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}F(y)\right|+\sum_{y\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}\left|\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x,y)dx-\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k,y)\right|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x,y)dxdy-\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}f(k)\right|\leq\left|\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d-1}}F(y)dy-\sum_{y\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}F(y)\right|+\sum_{y\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}\left|\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x,y)dx-\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k,y)\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the inductive hypothesis the first term is upper bounded by <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{d-1}/\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{d-1}/\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> for some constant <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{d-1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{d-1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since for every <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the function <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> is quasi-concave, one may use (<a href="#S3.E53" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>) to get that the second term is upper bounded by</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{y\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}\max_{x\in\mathbb{Z}}f(x,y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{y\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}\max_{x\in\mathbb{Z}}f(x,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">We conclude by Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem25" title="Lemma 25. ‣ 3.3 Sum of maxima of isotropic log-concave functions ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A remark from convex geometry: the case of isotropic convex bodies.</span> Applying the previous proposition to <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=\mathds{1}_{K}/|K|_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=\mathds{1}_{K}/|K|_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is an isotropic convex body in <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and using that, in this case, <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=L_{K}|K|^{1/d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=L_{K}|K|^{1/d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we deduce the following proposition.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem27" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem27.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 27</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem27.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem27.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem27.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem27.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any isotropic convex body <math id="Thmtheorem27.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="Thmtheorem27.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\frac{\#(K\cap\mathbb{Z}^{d})}{|K|_{d}}-1\right|\leq\frac{M_{d}}{|K|^{\frac{1}{d}}}\hskip 2.84544pt," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\frac{\#(K\cap\mathbb{Z}^{d})}{|K|_{d}}-1\right|\leq\frac{M_{d}}{|K|^{\frac{1}{d}}}\hskip 2.84544pt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem27.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem27.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for some constant <math id="Thmtheorem27.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{d}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{d}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, depending only on the dimension,
where <math id="Thmtheorem27.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\#K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#K</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the cardinality of a discrete set <math id="Thmtheorem27.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem28" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem28.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 28</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem28.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem28.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem28.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem28.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The hypothesis of isotropicity is necessary, since in <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>,
it is easy to construct convex bodies that do not contain integer points, but whose volumes are increasingly large.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem29" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem29.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 29</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem29.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem29.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem29.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem29.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem29.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a centered, isotropic, log-concave density. Then, for <math id="Thmtheorem29.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq d</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}k_{i}f(k)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}x_{i}f(x)dx+O_{d}(1)=O_{d}(1).\hskip 2.84544pt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}k_{i}f(k)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}x_{i}f(x)dx+O_{d}(1)=O_{d}(1).\hskip 2.84544pt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem29.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem29.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, for <math id="Thmtheorem29.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the following finite bound holds for any log-concave centered integrable function</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\int_{\mathbb{R}}xf(x)dx-\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}kf(k)\right|\leq(e+1)\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)\hskip 2.84544pt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\int_{\mathbb{R}}xf(x)dx-\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}kf(k)\right|\leq(e+1)\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)\hskip 2.84544pt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is by induction again. Let us make a one dimensional remark that will be used on the base case of the induction. Let <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a centered log-concave function and let suppose that the maximum of <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is attained at <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and let us suppose without loss of generality that <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then since <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave and by the inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, Theorem 4]</cite> one has</span></p>
<table id="S3.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x)dx\geq\int_{0}^{x_{0}}f(x)dx\geq f(0)x_{0}\geq\frac{\max f}{e}x_{0}\hskip 2.84544pt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mi>e</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x)dx\geq\int_{0}^{x_{0}}f(x)dx\geq f(0)x_{0}\geq\frac{\max f}{e}x_{0}\hskip 2.84544pt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, we get <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\max f\leq e\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\max f\leq e\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x)dx</annotation></semantics></math>. The case of the summation is analogous. Let <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}\in\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}\in\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> be such that <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}\leq x_{0}&lt;k_{0}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}\leq x_{0}&lt;k_{0}+1</annotation></semantics></math> . Then, we deduce</span></p>
<table id="S3.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)\geq\sum_{k=0}^{k_{0}}f(k)\geq(k_{0}+1)f(0)\geq\frac{\max f}{e}(k_{0}+1)\hskip 2.84544pt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mi>e</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)\geq\sum_{k=0}^{k_{0}}f(k)\geq(k_{0}+1)f(0)\geq\frac{\max f}{e}(k_{0}+1)\hskip 2.84544pt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let us start the induction. Let <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> be a centered, isotropic, log-concave density and let suppose that the maximum of <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is attained at <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. We decompose the integral <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}}xf(x)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}}xf(x)dx</annotation></semantics></math> as follows</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}}xf(x)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}}xf(x)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex112.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k&lt;0}\int_{k}^{k+1}xf(x)dx+\sum_{k=0}^{k_{0}-1}\int_{k}^{k+1}xf(x)dx+\int_{k_{0}}^{k_{0}+1}xf(x)dx+\sum_{k\geq k_{0}+1}\int_{k}^{k+1}xf(x)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k&lt;0}\int_{k}^{k+1}xf(x)dx+\sum_{k=0}^{k_{0}-1}\int_{k}^{k+1}xf(x)dx+\int_{k_{0}}^{k_{0}+1}xf(x)dx+\sum_{k\geq k_{0}+1}\int_{k}^{k+1}xf(x)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{k&lt;0}kf(k+1)+\sum_{k=0}^{k_{0}-1}kf(k)+k_{0}\min\{f(k_{0}),f(k_{0}+1)\}+\sum_{k\geq k_{0}+1}kf(k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{k&lt;0}kf(k+1)+\sum_{k=0}^{k_{0}-1}kf(k)+k_{0}\min\{f(k_{0}),f(k_{0}+1)\}+\sum_{k\geq k_{0}+1}kf(k+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
