<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">We observe that <math id="S3.SS4.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x_{0})=\max{f}\leq\frac{1}{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x_{0})=\max{f}\leq\frac{1}{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> and, by (<a href="#S3.E54" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a>), <math id="S3.SS4.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}=O({\sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}=O({\sigma})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the last term in (<a href="#S3.E56" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>)
is <math id="S3.SS4.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Furthermore, by Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem26" title="Proposition 26. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>, the second term in (<a href="#S3.E56" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>) is <math id="S3.SS4.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x)x^{2}dx\leq\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)k^{2}+O(\sigma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x)x^{2}dx\leq\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)k^{2}+O(\sigma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, using the piecewise monotonicity of <math id="S3.SS4.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> in the reverse way, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x)x^{2}dx\geq\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)k^{2}+O(\sigma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x)x^{2}dx\geq\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k)k^{2}+O(\sigma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">This proves the base case.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathbb{R}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathbb{R}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and let
<math id="S3.SS4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(y):=\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x,y)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(y):=\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x,y)dx</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, by the inductive hypothesis applied to <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,d-1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,d-1,</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S3.E57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x,y)y_{i}^{2}dxdy=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d-1}}F(y)y_{i}^{2}dy=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}F(k)k_{i}^{2}+O_{d}(\sigma)\hskip 2.84544pt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x,y)y_{i}^{2}dxdy=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d-1}}F(y)y_{i}^{2}dy=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}F(k)k_{i}^{2}+O_{d}(\sigma)\hskip 2.84544pt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since, for every <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the function <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot,k)</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave in <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have, by (<a href="#S3.E53" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="S3.E58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|F(k)-\sum_{k^{\prime}\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k^{\prime},k)\right|=\left|\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x,k)dx-\sum_{k^{\prime}\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k^{\prime},k)\right|\leq\max_{x}f(x,k)\hskip 2.84544pt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>x</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|F(k)-\sum_{k^{\prime}\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k^{\prime},k)\right|=\left|\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x,k)dx-\sum_{k^{\prime}\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k^{\prime},k)\right|\leq\max_{x}f(x,k)\hskip 2.84544pt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">So by (<a href="#S3.E57" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">57</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E58" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>) we get, for <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,d-1</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x,y)y_{i}^{2}dxdy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x,y)y_{i}^{2}dxdy</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex131.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k^{\prime}\in\mathbb{Z},k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}f(k^{\prime},k)k_{i}^{2}+\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}O(\max_{x}f(x,k))k_{i}^{2}+O_{d}(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>x</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k^{\prime}\in\mathbb{Z},k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}f(k^{\prime},k)k_{i}^{2}+\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}O(\max_{x}f(x,k))k_{i}^{2}+O_{d}(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k^{\prime}\in\mathbb{Z},k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}f(k^{\prime},k)k_{i}^{2}+O_{d}(\sigma)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k^{\prime}\in\mathbb{Z},k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}f(k^{\prime},k)k_{i}^{2}+O_{d}(\sigma),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">by Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem25" title="Lemma 25. ‣ 3.3 Sum of maxima of isotropic log-concave functions ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>, and the result follows.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p12.1" class="ltx_p">We will need the following lemma for the base case of the induction of Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem32" title="Proposition 32. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem31" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 31</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem31.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem31.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem31.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem31.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> be a centered, isotropic, log-concave density in <math id="Thmtheorem31.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="Thmtheorem31.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}{(f)}=\sigma^{2}\mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}{(f)}=\sigma^{2}\mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="Thmtheorem31.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, let</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\max}(x):=\inf\{y\in\mathbb{R}:f(x,y)=\max_{y}{f(x,y)}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>y</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\max}(x):=\inf\{y\in\mathbb{R}:f(x,y)=\max_{y}{f(x,y)}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem31.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem31.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="S3.E59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}}xN_{\max}(x)\max_{y}f(x,y)dx=O(\sigma)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>y</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}}xN_{\max}(x)\max_{y}f(x,y)dx=O(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem31.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem31.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="S3.E60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}{kN_{\max}(k)\max_{y}f(k,y)}=O(\sigma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>y</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}{kN_{\max}(k)\max_{y}f(k,y)}=O(\sigma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> be an absolute constant to be determined later and denote the set <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{\sigma}:=\{x\in\mathbb{R}:|x|,|N_{\max}(x)|\leq c\sigma\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\sigma}:=\{x\in\mathbb{R}:|x|,|N_{\max}(x)|\leq c\sigma\}.</annotation></semantics></math> We have</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}}xN_{\max}(x)\max_{y}f(x,y)dx=\int_{A_{\sigma}}xN_{\max}(x)\max_{y}f(x,y)dx+\int_{A_{\sigma}^{\mathrm{C}}}xN_{\max}(x)\max_{y}f(x,y)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>y</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>y</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>σ</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>y</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}}xN_{\max}(x)\max_{y}f(x,y)dx=\int_{A_{\sigma}}xN_{\max}(x)\max_{y}f(x,y)dx+\int_{A_{\sigma}^{\mathrm{C}}}xN_{\max}(x)\max_{y}f(x,y)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">The first term can be trivially bounded as</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl|\int_{A_{\sigma}}xN_{\max}(x)\max_{y}f(x,y)dx\Bigr|\leq O(\sigma^{3})\max{f}=O(\sigma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>y</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl|\int_{A_{\sigma}}xN_{\max}(x)\max_{y}f(x,y)dx\Bigr|\leq O(\sigma^{3})\max{f}=O(\sigma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p13.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p13.3.1" class="ltx_text">For the second term we have, for some absolute constant <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and for <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> large enough,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex136"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Bigl|\int_{A_{\sigma}^{\mathrm{C}}}|x|N_{\max}(x)\max_{y}f(x,y)dx\Bigr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>σ</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>y</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Bigl|\int_{A_{\sigma}^{\mathrm{C}}}|x|N_{\max}(x)\max_{y}f(x,y)dx\Bigr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex136.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\max(f)\int_{A_{\sigma}^{\mathrm{C}}}{xN_{\max}(x)e^{-\frac{|x|+N_{\max}(x)}{\sigma}C^{\prime}_{2}}dx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>σ</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\max(f)\int_{A_{\sigma}^{\mathrm{C}}}{xN_{\max}(x)e^{-\frac{|x|+N_{\max}(x)}{\sigma}C^{\prime}_{2}}dx}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq O\Bigl(\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}}\Bigr)\sigma\int_{x&gt;c\sigma}{xe^{-\frac{x}{\sigma}C^{\prime}_{2}}dx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq O\Bigl(\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}}\Bigr)\sigma\int_{x&gt;c\sigma}{xe^{-\frac{x}{\sigma}C^{\prime}_{2}}dx}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
