<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p13.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p13.4.1" class="ltx_text">Here (<a href="#S3.E61" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>) follows by using the fact that <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ye^{-y}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ye^{-y}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives (<a href="#S3.E59" title="In Lemma 31. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>),
(<a href="#S3.E60" title="In Lemma 31. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>) follows in a similar way.
∎</span></p>
