<p id="S3.SS4.p14.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p14.6.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows by Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem31" title="Lemma 31. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>.
On the other hand, for the second term in (<a href="#S3.E65" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">65</span></a>) we have</span></p>
