</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p14.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p14.7.1" class="ltx_text">by the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality and Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem30" title="Proposition 30. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>.
Finally, the third term in (<a href="#S3.E65" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">65</span></a>) is</span></p>
<table id="S3.E69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}}{\max_{y}f(x,y)(N_{\max}(x)+1)dx}=O(\sigma)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>y</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}}{\max_{y}f(x,y)(N_{\max}(x)+1)dx}=O(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p14.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p14.8.1" class="ltx_text">by Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem31" title="Lemma 31. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>.
Plugging (<a href="#S3.E67" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">67</span></a>), (<a href="#S3.E68" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E69" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>) into (<a href="#S3.E65" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">65</span></a>) we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S3.E70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2}}{f(x,y)xydx}\leq\sum_{k\geq 0}\sum_{m\geq 0}{kmf(m,k)}+\sum_{k\geq 0}{\sum_{m\geq 0}{kf(m,k)}}+O(\sigma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2}}{f(x,y)xydx}\leq\sum_{k\geq 0}\sum_{m\geq 0}{kmf(m,k)}+\sum_{k\geq 0}{\sum_{m\geq 0}{kf(m,k)}}+O(\sigma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p14.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p14.9.1" class="ltx_text">Using the reverse bounds to those in (<a href="#S3.E63" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">63</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E64" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">64</span></a>) obtained by the monotonicity of <math id="S3.SS4.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, we get
the lower bound</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex142" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
