<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p14.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p14.11.1" class="ltx_text">Since, by Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem29" title="Proposition 29. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>, <math id="S3.SS4.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}{\sum_{m}{kf(m,k)}}=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}{\sum_{m}{kf(m,k)}}=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, by adding (<a href="#S3.E70" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>)–(<a href="#S3.E73" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{2}}{f(x,y)xydx}=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}\sum_{m\in\mathbb{Z}}{kmf(m,k)}+O(\sigma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{2}}{f(x,y)xydx}=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}\sum_{m\in\mathbb{Z}}{kmf(m,k)}+O(\sigma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p14.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p14.12.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the base case <math id="S3.SS4.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">The inductive step is similar to that in the proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem30" title="Proposition 30. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>. Let <math id="S3.SS4.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{d-1})\in\mathbb{R}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{d-1})\in\mathbb{R}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and let
<math id="S3.SS4.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(y):=\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x,y)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(y):=\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x,y)dx</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, by the inductive hypothesis, for <math id="S3.SS4.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i,j\leq d-1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i,j\leq d-1,</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S3.E74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x,y)y_{i}y_{j}dy=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d-1}}F(y)y_{i}y_{j}dy=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}F(k)k_{i}k_{j}+O_{d}(\sigma)\hskip 2.84544pt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x,y)y_{i}y_{j}dy=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d-1}}F(y)y_{i}y_{j}dy=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}F(k)k_{i}k_{j}+O_{d}(\sigma)\hskip 2.84544pt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since for every <math id="S3.SS4.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=(k_{1},\ldots,k_{d-1})\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=(k_{1},\ldots,k_{d-1})\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the function <math id="S3.SS4.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot,k)</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave <math id="S3.SS4.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have by Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem26" title="Proposition 26. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a></span></p>
<table id="S3.E75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(k)-\sum_{k^{\prime}\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k^{\prime},k)=\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x,k)dx-\sum_{k^{\prime}\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k^{\prime},k)=O_{d}\bigl(\max_{x}f(x,k)\bigr)\hskip 2.84544pt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>x</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(k)-\sum_{k^{\prime}\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k^{\prime},k)=\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x,k)dx-\sum_{k^{\prime}\in\mathbb{Z}}f(k^{\prime},k)=O_{d}\bigl(\max_{x}f(x,k)\bigr)\hskip 2.84544pt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">So by (<a href="#S3.E74" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">74</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E75" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">75</span></a>) we get, for <math id="S3.SS4.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i,j\leq d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i,j\leq d-1</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S3.E76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x,y)y_{i}y_{j}dxdy=\sum_{k^{\prime}\in\mathbb{Z},k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}f(k^{\prime},k)k_{i}k_{j}+\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}O\Bigl(\max_{x}f(x,k)\Bigr)k_{i}k_{j}+O_{d}(\sigma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>x</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x,y)y_{i}y_{j}dxdy=\sum_{k^{\prime}\in\mathbb{Z},k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}f(k^{\prime},k)k_{i}k_{j}+\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}O\Bigl(\max_{x}f(x,k)\Bigr)k_{i}k_{j}+O_{d}(\sigma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p15.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p15.4.1" class="ltx_text">But by the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality and Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem25" title="Lemma 25. ‣ 3.3 Sum of maxima of isotropic log-concave functions ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>, <math id="S3.SS4.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}O\Bigl(\max_{x}f(x,k)\Bigr)k_{i}k_{j}=O_{d}(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}O\Bigl(\max_{x}f(x,k)\Bigr)k_{i}k_{j}=O_{d}(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> and the result follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem33" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem33.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 33</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem33.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem33.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem33.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem33.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem33.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> be a centered, isotropic, log-concave density in <math id="Thmtheorem33.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="Thmtheorem33.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}{(f)}=\sigma^{2}\mathrm{I}_{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}{(f)}=\sigma^{2}\mathrm{I}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math> Then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det\Bigl(\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}{(f)}\Bigr)=\sigma^{2d}+O_{d}(\sigma^{2d-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det\Bigl(\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}{(f)}\Bigr)=\sigma^{2d}+O_{d}(\sigma^{2d-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS4.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem32" title="Proposition 32. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a></span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex145" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}(f)]_{ij}=O_{d}(\sigma),\quad\text{for }i\neq j" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}(f)]_{ij}=O_{d}(\sigma),\quad\text{for }i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex146" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}(f)]_{ij}=\sigma^{2}+O_{d}(\sigma),\quad\text{for }i=j." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}(f)]_{ij}=\sigma^{2}+O_{d}(\sigma),\quad\text{for }i=j.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p16.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p16.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex147"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\det\Bigl(\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}{(f)}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\det\Bigl(\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}{(f)}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex147.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\tau}\mathrm{sgn}(\tau)\prod_{i=1}^{d}\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}(f)_{i\tau(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>τ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>sgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\tau}\mathrm{sgn}(\tau)\prod_{i=1}^{d}\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}(f)_{i\tau(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex148"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma^{2d}+O(\sigma^{2d-1})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma^{2d}+O(\sigma^{2d-1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p16.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p16.4.1" class="ltx_text">since for <math id="S3.SS4.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> being the identity permutation <math id="S3.SS4.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{sgn}(\tau)\prod_{i=1}^{d}{\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}{(f)}_{i\tau(i)}}=\bigl(\sigma^{2}+O(\sigma)\bigr)^{d}=\sigma^{2d}+O(\sigma^{2d-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>sgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{sgn}(\tau)\prod_{i=1}^{d}{\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}{(f)}_{i\tau(i)}}=\bigl(\sigma^{2}+O(\sigma)\bigr)^{d}=\sigma^{2d}+O(\sigma^{2d-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and for any other permutation <math id="S3.SS4.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex149" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{i=1}^{d}{\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}{(f)}_{i\tau^{\prime}(i)}}=O((\sigma^{2})^{d-2}\sigma^{2})=O_{d}(\sigma^{2d-2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i=1}^{d}{\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{Z}^{d}}{(f)}_{i\tau^{\prime}(i)}}=O((\sigma^{2})^{d-2}\sigma^{2})=O_{d}(\sigma^{2d-2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p16.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p16.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p17.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem34" title="Corollary 34 (Theorem for isotropic 𝑓). ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a> below is a version of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 7. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> with the assumption that the continuous function <math id="S3.SS4.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is isotropic.
It can be seen that due to use of Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem33" title="Corollary 33. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>, <math id="S3.SS4.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> needs to be taken at least <math id="S3.SS4.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(d!)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(d!)</annotation></semantics></math>. We do not know whether this is the best (lowest) rate.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem34" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem34.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 34</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem34.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmtheorem34.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 7. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> for isotropic <math id="Thmtheorem34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem34.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem34.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem34.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem34.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> be log-concave p.m.f. on <math id="Thmtheorem34.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, whose continuous log-concave extension, say <math id="Thmtheorem34.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, is isotropic. Then there exists an absolute constant <math id="Thmtheorem34.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>
such that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex150" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
