<div id="S3.SS4.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS4.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is extensible log-concave, there exists a continuous log-concave function <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> (not necessarily a density) such that <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(k)=p(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(k)=p(k)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and by assumption <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is isotropic. Thus</span></p>
<table id="S3.E77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}p(k)\leq\max_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x)=\frac{L_{f}^{d}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f}{\sigma^{d}}\leq\frac{C\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}{f}}{\sigma^{d}}\hskip 2.84544pt," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}p(k)\leq\max_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x)=\frac{L_{f}^{d}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f}{\sigma^{d}}\leq\frac{C\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}{f}}{\sigma^{d}}\hskip 2.84544pt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is an upper bound of <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{f}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{f}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be taken to be an absolute constant as guaranteed by the Isotropic Constant Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem 9. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.
Noting that by definition <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}{(Zp)}=\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}{(Zp)}=\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}</annotation></semantics></math> for any normalizing constant <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\in\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\in\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and applying Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem26" title="Proposition 26. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a> and Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem33" title="Corollary 33. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a> to <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{f(\cdot)}{\int{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">f</mi></mrow></mstyle></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{f(\cdot)}{\int{f}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex151" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}p(k)\leq\frac{C(1+O_{d}(\frac{1}{\sigma}))}{\Bigl(\det\Bigl(\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}\Bigr)+O_{d}(\sigma^{2d-1})\Bigr)^{1/2}}\leq\frac{2C}{\det\Bigl(\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}\Bigr)^{\frac{1}{2}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}p(k)\leq\frac{C(1+O_{d}(\frac{1}{\sigma}))}{\Bigl(\det\Bigl(\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}\Bigr)+O_{d}(\sigma^{2d-1})\Bigr)^{1/2}}\leq\frac{2C}{\det\Bigl(\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}\Bigr)^{\frac{1}{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p18.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p18.3.1" class="ltx_text">provided that <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is large enough depending on <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, using that <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O_{d}(\sigma^{2d-1})\geq-\frac{1}{4}\det\Bigl(\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}\Bigr)\simeq-\frac{1}{4}\sigma^{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≃</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{d}(\sigma^{2d-1})\geq-\frac{1}{4}\det\Bigl(\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}\Bigr)\simeq-\frac{1}{4}\sigma^{2d}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that implicitly we also used <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int{f}=O_{d}(\sum_{k}{f(k)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int{f}=O_{d}(\sum_{k}{f(k)})</annotation></semantics></math> (for <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> not necessarily a density) which can be seen directly from the proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem26" title="Proposition 26. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>. The result follows with <math id="S3.SS4.p18.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}=2C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}=2C</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
