<div id="S3.SS4.9" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS4.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any one-dimensional quasi-concave non-negative real sequence <math id="S3.SS4.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{n})_{n\in\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{n})_{n\in\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n\in\mathbb{Z}}|a_{n}-a_{n-1}|\leq 2\max_{n\in\mathbb{Z}}a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n\in\mathbb{Z}}|a_{n}-a_{n-1}|\leq 2\max_{n\in\mathbb{Z}}a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, by log-concavity, denoting <math id="S3.SS4.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{k_{i}}=\sum_{j\neq i}k_{j}e_{j}\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{k_{i}}=\sum_{j\neq i}k_{j}e_{j}\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex153" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}|p(k)-p(k-e_{i})|\leq 2\sum_{\overline{k_{i}}\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}\max_{k_{i}\in\mathbb{Z}}p(k_{1},\ldots,k_{i-1},k_{i},k_{i+1},\ldots,k_{d})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo fence="false" lspace="0.278em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{d}}|p(k)-p(k-e_{i})|\leq 2\sum_{\overline{k_{i}}\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}\max_{k_{i}\in\mathbb{Z}}p(k_{1},\ldots,k_{i-1},k_{i},k_{i+1},\ldots,k_{d}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, as in (<a href="#S3.E52" title="In Lemma 25. ‣ 3.3 Sum of maxima of isotropic log-concave functions ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex154" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\overline{k_{i}}\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}\max_{k_{i}\in\mathbb{Z}}p(k_{1},\ldots,k_{i-1},k_{i},k_{i+1},\ldots,k_{d})=O_{d}\Bigl(\frac{1}{\det{\bigl(\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}\bigr)^{\frac{1}{2d}}}}\Bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\overline{k_{i}}\in\mathbb{Z}^{d-1}}\max_{k_{i}\in\mathbb{Z}}p(k_{1},\ldots,k_{i-1},k_{i},k_{i+1},\ldots,k_{d})=O_{d}\Bigl(\frac{1}{\det{\bigl(\mathrm{Cov}{(p)}\bigr)^{\frac{1}{2d}}}}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p19.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p19.3.1" class="ltx_text">and the result follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p20.1" class="ltx_p">We are ready to give the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem20" title="Theorem 20. ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.10" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem20" title="Theorem 20. ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS4.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">Part <a href="#S3.I1.i1" title="item 1 ‣ Theorem 20. ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> follows directly from Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem34" title="Corollary 34 (Theorem for isotropic 𝑓). ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a> (in fact with <math id="S3.SS4.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}(d)</annotation></semantics></math> being independent of the dimension <math id="S3.SS4.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>). Part <a href="#S3.I1.i2" title="item 2 ‣ Theorem 20. ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> follows from Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem24" title="Lemma 24 (Concentration Lemma). ‣ 3.2 A concentration lemma ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>, the well-known fact that for a centered log-concave function <math id="S3.SS4.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.SS4.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex155" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(0)\simeq_{d}\frac{1}{\det{(\mathrm{Cov}(f))^{\frac{1}{2}}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>≃</mo><mi>d</mi></msub><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(0)\simeq_{d}\frac{1}{\det{(\mathrm{Cov}(f))^{\frac{1}{2}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p21.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p21.2.1" class="ltx_text">and Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem33" title="Corollary 33. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>. Finally, Part <a href="#S3.I1.i3" title="item 3 ‣ Theorem 20. ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> follows directly from Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem35" title="Proposition 35. ‣ 3.4 Approximating the integral, mean and covariance discretely ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5 </span>Relaxing the isotropicity assumption on <math id="S3.SS5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we relax the assumptions of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem23" title="Lemma 23. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>, so that we obtain conclusions of the same kind under some weaker assumptions on the eigenvalues of the continuous covariance matrix <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{R}}{(f)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbb{R}}{(f)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, we will prove:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem36" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem36.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 36</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem36.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem36.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem36.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem36.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every centered and log-concave density <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and for every <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> one has</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex156" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}^{d+2}f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}\sqrt{\lambda_{\min}(\mathrm{Cov}(f))}\leq\left(\int_{0}^{\infty}r^{d-1}f(r\theta)dr\right)^{\frac{1}{d}}\leq(d+1)c_{2}^{d+2}f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}\sqrt{\lambda_{\max}(\mathrm{Cov}(f))}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}^{d+2}f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}\sqrt{\lambda_{\min}(\mathrm{Cov}(f))}\leq\left(\int_{0}^{\infty}r^{d-1}f(r\theta)dr\right)^{\frac{1}{d}}\leq(d+1)c_{2}^{d+2}f(0)^{\frac{1}{d}}\sqrt{\lambda_{\max}(\mathrm{Cov}(f))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem36.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem36.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem36.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are the constants appearing in (<a href="#S3.E43" title="In Definition 21. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Before giving the proof, we mention the consequences of Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem36" title="Proposition 36. ‣ 3.5 Relaxing the isotropicity assumption on 𝑓 ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem37" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem37.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 37</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem37.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem37.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem37.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem37.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> be a a centered, almost isotropic log-concave density. Then for every <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex157" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\infty}r^{d-1}f(r\theta)dr=\Theta_{d}(1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\infty}r^{d-1}f(r\theta)dr=\Theta_{d}(1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem37.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem37.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">as <math id="Thmtheorem37.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma:=\det{(\mathrm{Cov}{(f)})}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma:=\det{(\mathrm{Cov}{(f)})}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is almost isotropic, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex158" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{min}}\big(\mathrm{Cov}(f)\big)\simeq_{d}\lambda_{\mathrm{max}}\big(\mathrm{Cov}(f)\big)\simeq_{d}\sigma^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>≃</mo><mi>d</mi></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>≃</mo><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{min}}\big(\mathrm{Cov}(f)\big)\simeq_{d}\lambda_{\mathrm{max}}\big(\mathrm{Cov}(f)\big)\simeq_{d}\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">as <math id="S3.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. The result follows from Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem36" title="Proposition 36. ‣ 3.5 Relaxing the isotropicity assumption on 𝑓 ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a> since <math id="S3.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(0)\simeq_{d}\max{f}\simeq_{d}\frac{1}{\sigma^{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>≃</mo><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>max</mi><mi>f</mi><msub><mo>≃</mo><mi>d</mi></msub><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(0)\simeq_{d}\max{f}\simeq_{d}\frac{1}{\sigma^{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem38" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem38.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 38</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem38.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem38.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem38.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem38.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The isotropicity assumption was only used in Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem23" title="Lemma 23. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>, which in turn allowed us to prove the concentration Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem24" title="Lemma 24 (Concentration Lemma). ‣ 3.2 A concentration lemma ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a> which was repeatedly evoked in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> to bound the sums of maxima of log-concave functions and thus also the error terms. By Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem37" title="Corollary 37. ‣ 3.5 Relaxing the isotropicity assumption on 𝑓 ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>, a version of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem24" title="Lemma 24 (Concentration Lemma). ‣ 3.2 A concentration lemma ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a> holds true for almost isotropic densities, although with possibly different constants and for large enough <math id="Thmtheorem38.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, all the previous results of Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> hold true and thus also the statements of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 1.2 Main results and paper outline ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> under the almost isotropic log-concave assumption.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem39" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem39.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 39</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem39.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem39.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem39.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem39.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Note that if the function <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is in addition isotropic i.e.
<math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}{(f)}=\sigma^{2}\mathrm{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}{(f)}=\sigma^{2}\mathrm{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has that <math id="Thmtheorem39.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(0)\simeq_{d}\frac{1}{\sigma^{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>≃</mo><mi>d</mi></msub><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(0)\simeq_{d}\frac{1}{\sigma^{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> and so we recover the result of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem23" title="Lemma 23. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For the above-mentioned proposition, the following lemma which gives bounds for the inradius and circumradius of convex bodies in not necessarily isotropic position will be essential .</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem36" title="Proposition 36. ‣ 3.5 Relaxing the isotropicity assumption on 𝑓 ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a centered log-concave density. For simplicity, we denote <math id="S3.SS5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}=\lambda_{\min}(\mathrm{Cov}(f))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}=\lambda_{\min}(\mathrm{Cov}(f))</annotation></semantics></math> and analogously for <math id="S3.SS5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>. Following the same steps as in the proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem23" title="Lemma 23. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>, we get that, for any <math id="S3.SS5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\lambda_{\min}}{f(0)}\leq\int_{K_{d+2}(f)}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx=\frac{1}{f(0)}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}f(x)dx\leq\frac{\lambda_{\max}}{f(0)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\lambda_{\min}}{f(0)}\leq\int_{K_{d+2}(f)}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx=\frac{1}{f(0)}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}f(x)dx\leq\frac{\lambda_{\max}}{f(0)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using the inclusion relations (<a href="#S3.E43" title="In Definition 21. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>), this gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex160" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}^{2d+2}\lambda_{\min}\leq\frac{1}{|K_{d+1}(f)|}\int_{K_{d+1}(f)}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx\leq c_{2}^{2d+2}\lambda_{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}^{2d+2}\lambda_{\min}\leq\frac{1}{|K_{d+1}(f)|}\int_{K_{d+1}(f)}\langle x,u\rangle^{2}dx\leq c_{2}^{2d+2}\lambda_{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using these inequalities, (<a href="#S3.E48" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>) and again the inclusion relations (<a href="#S3.E43" title="In Definition 21. ‣ 3.1 Ball’s bodies ‣ 3 Discrete isotropic log-concave random vectors ‣ On the monotonicity of discrete entropy for log-concave random vectors on ℤ^𝑑" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>), we get</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex161" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
